 "doc": "Premise of Proposition 1 (SSOT 10.18.426, CCC request item 7): is the class prior pi approximately the stationary distribution of M?\npi and M are the decoders' own training statistics (add-one counts, training labels only): macd.iemocap_training_stats /\nmacd.meld_training_stats / m3.train_stats, and the three recency matrices M^(b) built as in paper2_rrtdV_20260924.py.\nFor every deployment unit (IEMOCAP-4 / IEMOCAP-6 folds 1-5, MELD, M3ED) and every matrix:\n  pi*            stationary distribution of the matrix (left eigenvector of eigenvalue 1)\n  TV             0.5 * sum |pi - pi*|\n  max_rel        max_c |pi*(c) - pi(c)| / pi(c)\n  KL             KL(pi || pi*)\n  max_log_ratio  max_c |log((pi M)(c) / pi(c))|: the belief of Proposition 1 when the previous belief is pi instead of pi*\n                 equals p_t(c) * (pi M)(c) / pi(c) up to normalisation, so this is the size of the deviation from p_t(c)\n  prior_log_range log(max pi / min pi): for contrast, the spread of the factor pi(c) that the uncorrected product multiplies in\nCPU only, no model scores read.  Usage: script.py",
